WEBVTT

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:06.130
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.420
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.400
<b>E-genes</b>

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.000
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.740
<b>AU balls</b>

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:17.770
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.370
and embody AU weapons.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:27.110
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.020
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.510
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.290
Gun No. 3: Capa's Island!

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.690
<b>Drool </b>

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.690
We'll be arriving at our 
destination momentarily.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.700
<b>A girl who drools</b>

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.640
Please return your seat backs 
to their upright positions.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.740
Ugh, so muggy.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.640
Shoulda brought summer clothes.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.970
A Humvee!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.970
<b>Humvee 
A High Mobility 
Multipurpose 
Wheeled Vehicle.</b>

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.810
Well then, let us be on our way.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:46.990
Okay!

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.180
I wonder if we should really be 
entrusting her to him so soon...

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:02.000
But if she can't overcome this trial,
we can't possibly throw her into battle.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.380
Am I wrong?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.820
No, you're right.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:11.500
This is just what we have 
to expect of her...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.980
...as a sniper.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:18.990
We've arrived.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.530
Right!

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.550
Please wait a moment.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.060
Ah, bu— wait!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.700
Aw, man.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.630
D-Don't leave me!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.170
Catch!

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.620
M-My gun!

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.200
D-Dammit! Hit 'em!

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.340
You score a zero.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.890
Huh?! I thought I was 
done-for back there, but...

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:53.460
All that just now was a reproduction 
created by my AU weapon.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.510
This is a Dogoo training facility.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.360
Hey, Saint-Germain.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.320
Yes, sir.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:08.290
Did this girl really kill 
200 Objects in Taiwan?

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.490
I believe you have 
seen the data.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.690
That digital stuff? 
Can't trust it.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.720
In the end, we can only 
rely on analog.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:21.230
We'd like to have you take 
charge of her education.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.740
Commander's orders.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.720
No worries. I'll do the work 
I'm getting paid for.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.670
Besides, this is the perfect job for a fellow 
who's been taken off the roster.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.850
It was all for training, 
but I apologize.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:52.190
I'm the unfortunate man who's been tasked 
with your education, Robert Capa.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.070
Capa? You mean the 
war photographer?

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:59.970
Hit the sack for today. 
Your real training begins tomorrow.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.920
Oh, right. I gotta send my mom 
a pic, and then...

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.210
I wonder if Asao's been released 
from the hospital.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.650
<b>No signal</b>

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.020
Out of range?!

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.950
That's right. Inside Dogoo 
administration zone,

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.640
personal communications are restricted.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.910
How is a modern-day high school girl supposed 
to get by with no phone or Net?!

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:39.440
You're not a modern-day high school girl, 
you're a member of Dogoo.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.750
And the commander has high hopes for you.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.730
Is it an urgent matter?

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.730
No, not really.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.490
Ugh, I'm so pissed off!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.070
<b>Bedhead </b>

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.650
<b>Drool </b>

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.140
Ummm...

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.410
I came here for... training, was it?

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.980
I wonder if I can do this...

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.720
Whadaya think you're doin'?!

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:33.170
Get dressed and get 
yer butt down here!

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.930
<b>Chalk</b>

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:34.520
Okay.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:36.900
I'd like a proper response!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.770
<i>Sir! Yes, sir!</i>

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:55.410
Dammit! 
Dammitdammitdammitdammitdammit!

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.190
All right!

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.970
Nothing's "all right."

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:02.360
Hitting them at point-blank 
is no training at all!

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:06.400
The job of a shooter class holder 
is to snipe enemies at range.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:07.670
Sure, but...

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.410
Keep your eyes on the enemy!

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.430
If you're gonna puke, 
do it in a bucket.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.300
<b>Bucket girl</b>

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.350
12 laps to go!

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.210
Why is this... part of my training?

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.600
You may be an E-gene holder,

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.920
but in using your body to fight an enemy,
 you're no different from a common soldier.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.690
Next is classroom studies.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.360
What? Lemme have just 
a little break...

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.450
The commander has high hopes for you.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:50.840
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:56.900
Various effects are observed in holders 
at the time of AU weapon engagement:

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:00.690
enhanced physical abilities, and, though 
it varies according to the individual,

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.000
a mental rush, etc. Furthermore...

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.630
Remember the commander's hopes...

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.040
Are you awake now?

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:18.480
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.090
Today's Friday, huh...

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.560
You mean her boyfriend?

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.450
Aw, I'm so jealous! 

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:44.110
Maybe things were more 
fun at school...

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.540
How mean!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.050
Shh, jeez.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.860
I came here prepared 
to die to save the world,

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:07.410
but no phone or e-mail 
is just insane.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.600
An antenna? Well yeah, they'd have 
to have communications equipment.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.580
Over there!

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:25.120
An E-767, with the airborne early 
warning and control system!

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.970
<b>E-767
A plane with AEW&C 
developed by Boeing.</b>

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.770
<b>US-2
A rescue plane used 
by the Maritime 
Self Defense Force.</b>

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.390
They even have a Self Defense Force US-2!

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.300
Oh yeah, gotta take pictures!

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.230
This is crazy!

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:08.890
No...

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.350
U-uh— I— um—

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.940
Excuse me!

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.460
Miss Ogura?

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.440
Yessss?

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:29.560
It's an honor to meet you.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.390
O-Oh...

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:38.060
I... I saw the recording of 
your battle in Taiwan.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.350
It was just amazing.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:42.980
Could I get your autograph for 
my mother out in the country?

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.980
Uh... 

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:46.130
Would you like a banana sent 
from my hometown?

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.130
Umm... 

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:47.870
Oh, excuse me.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:53.190
I'm Harold S. Conway, 
2nd Lt. in the U.S. Air Force.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.050
The U.S. Armed Forces...?

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:57.220
I'm with the Australian Defence Force!

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:58.420
I'm from Canada!

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.300
From Japan!

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:04.090
Philippines here! 
Oh, please have a banana!

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.680
Don't be ridiculous! Japanese people 
should eat Japanese food!

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.660
<b>Mito Natto </b>

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.890
From me, a kiwi!

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.140
Your autograph! 

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.460
Sorry about that.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:19.370
Everyone is just so excited 
to meet you, Nobunagun.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:23.720
But... you're all from the armies 
of different countries?

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:28.270
Yes. On this base, we're mainly doing ocean 
observation and special duty ship maintenance.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.150
We also take care of supplying <i>Alex Logan.</i>

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:34.150
<i>Alex Logan</i>...?

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.410
You'll learn soon enough.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:38.610
Oh...

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.440
This is my unit's pride and joy.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:48.990
This is... a variation on the C-130? 
Or an HC— I mean, SC?

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:46.950
<b>C-130
A transport aircraft 
made by Lockheed.</b>

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.370
<b>HC-130
The combat search 
and rescue version.</b>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.450
<b>SC-130
The search and 
rescue version.</b>

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.100
It's a WC-130J.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.080
<b>WC-130J
The weather 
reconnaissance version.</b>

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.100
You mean... 
are you Hurricane Hunters?!

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.720
You've heard of us?

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.690
You b-b-bet I have!

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:02.920
The fearless badasses who fly into 
hurricanes to take meteorological observations!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.170
Aw, don't make me blush.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:09.330
We can chase the wind in this baby.

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:15.280
To think that I would see a real 
one in a place like this...

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.800
"A place like this," huh? 
Well, I guess it is...

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.810
Ah, sorry. I just don't see anybody 
when I go to the cafeteria, and...

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:28.590
E-gene holders are VIPs. 
We're not allowed to mingle.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.520
Really?

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:36.000
If it's not a bother, we'd love to have 
a meal with you sometime.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.100
Sure!

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.770
Three laps left! Make 'em count!

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.150
This is rough...

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.100
Th-They're watching me!

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:08.240
<b>E-gene [holder]
AU ball ——> AU weapon </b>

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.880
Theoretically, it should be possible 
for an E-gene holder

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.260
to use their powers without 
an AU ball. However...

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.650
Seems like your training is 
pretty rough. Are you all right?

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:24.280
I just keep messing up...

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:26.050
No way!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.310
E-gene holders are the only ones who can 
beat the Evolutionary Invasion Objects,

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:32.950
so have more confidence!

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.570
Y-You think I should?

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:36.560
Eat this so you'll be 
strong out there!

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:37.860
Mine, too! 

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:39.320
Here you go!

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.540
Nobunagun, ready to go!

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:53.850
But why "Nobunagun" and not "Nobunaga"?

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.370
Well, it's cooler that way, isn't it?

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.360
Mm, whatever.

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:08.080
By the way, it seems like you're getting 
chummy with the soldiers...

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:10.900
Oh, yeah. They're all 
such good people.

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:12.880
What they are is a shield.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:14.640
A shield?

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:20.490
In the battle against Evolutionary Invasion Objects, 
E-gene holders are our only asset.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:22.990
Those guys are just a shield 
for your protection.

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:25.710
Th-That's a horrible way to put it...

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:28.180
And if they can't hack it as a shield, 
they'll be sacrificed.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.630
At the very end of the 
battle in Taiwan,

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:34.890
if you had been able to shoot 
that infantry class Object,

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:37.650
you might have contained 
the damage.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:44.650
You didn't come here 
to make friends.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:45.640
Got it?

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:52.720
Good... I like that face.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:57.680
Ow!

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.680
Wha—?! Huh?!

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.290
These are your opponents for today.

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:13.240
Take your anger at screwing up 
in Taiwan out on yourself.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.940
If you take them lightly 'cause they're copies,
 you'll get yourself killed.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.360
I'm in—?!

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:31.540
I thought you seemed lonely, 
so I put in a little extra effort.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:35.700
If you're used to the area, you should be 
able to use the terrain to your advantage, right?

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:42.010
Can't you hurry it up a bit?

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:45.270
I wanna eat.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:51.850
You think you can hit 'em like that?! 
Don't just spit bullets; aim and fire!

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.720
Aim and...

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:57.880
At your skill level, just shooting a lot 
doesn't mean you'll connect.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:00.080
You're just using up your energy!

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.320
Aim, aim!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.760
I'm not hitting 'em.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:12.220
Reign in the power! The recoil is jerking 
your center off balance.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:17.080
You're the one who designs 
your AU weapon!

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.510
Even the explosive power of 
the bullets is up to you!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.790
You can say that, but...

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:35.070
...there's just no way!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.720
Hey, c'mon, get it together.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:44.040
If we have too much free time, 
I'll do something naughty.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:54.500
What do you think you're doing?!

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:55.750
Oh...?

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.660
So you can hit something 
if it's sitting still.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.310
But the enemy moves.

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:06.670
Predict the enemy's movements. 
Focus on their future position.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.670
Aim at where they <i>will</i> be.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:11.560
Reign in the power.

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:16.680
Aim and shoot. 
No rapid fire.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.590
Predict the enemy's moves.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.190
Fire!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:26.930
Noooooo!

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.000
Miss Ogura!

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:34.500
Y-Yes?

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.340
Thank you!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.010
B-But... I didn't...

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:42.920
To go out of your way (and your clothes) 
to do this for us is just... {TB: They're punning a Japanese idiom for lend a hand which is "take off a layer of skin."}

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.630
Wha—! Bu—! I—!

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.140
What the heck?!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.180
Th-They're wonderful!

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.620
I'm declaring these 
family heirlooms!

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:53.650
<b>Not her real boob</b>

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:53.650
<b>'shopped?</b>

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.940
Ah, hold on a sec!

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:02.240
Hm? Eat yer grub 
and get to bed.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.290
W-W-What's up with 
this picture?!

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.590
Ah, I went ahead and took 
them with your copies.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:14.000
Nice shots, don't you think? Yep, in 
the end we can only rely on analog.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.420
Those guys could use a little 
spice in their lives, right?

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:24.390
But you were saying all that awful stuff 
earlier about shields and sacrifice...

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:27.000
That was to screw your 
head on straight.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.200
You think I'd really say those things 
about my comrades in arms?

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:31.130
Hey!

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:35.110
You... You...

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:37.580
You won't get away with this!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:44.750
Well then, we're off.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.970
Bye! Take care!

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.710
How cool!

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:03.700
I'd sure like to see "how cool" you can be.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:08.110
At the rate you're going, you may be unable 
to live up to the commander's hopes.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.100
Let's go. Back to basics today.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:13.300
Gotcha...

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:20.620
This is D-101. We're currently 
passing over Mexico,

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:22.360
and should enter the storm 
zone momentarily.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:28.310
Her name is Olga. 
Our first big beauty in a while.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:31.090
But not as beautiful as Miss Ogura.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.710
Okay, let's ride that wind!

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:35.730
Aye!

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:48.030
The radar's picked up something, 
from the center of the hurricane!

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:52.400
It's a crazy storm with 
60 m/s winds up ahead!

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.850
What kind of idiot's out in that?!

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:57.390
Can't determine IFF! No metal detected!

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.780
Is this a...?!

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:29.590
Robert Capa, Nobunagun, 
please suspend training.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:30.220
Oh, boy...

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.060
This is an emergency.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:36.050
It appears that D-101 was shot down 
while observing the hurricane.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.850
A helicopter is currently standing 
by for transfer.

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:42.830
Robert Capa and Nobunagun, 
please board immediately.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:45.730
N...

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:47.360
No...

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:50.170
No way...

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.880
Hey, you know Hurricane?

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:30.190
Oh, that jellyfish monster, right?!

00:23:30.740 --> 00:23:33.410
Is this one of those Japanese otaku 
you always hear about?

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:34.420
Huh?

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:37.160
Next time, Gun No. 4: 
"Hurricane."

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:38.930
Ya better watch it!
